1. System Architecture
The UGIRAP NephraCore™ platform integrates a Micro-Electromechanical Systems (MEMS) synthetic hemofiltration module, a photoelectrocatalytic (PEC) urea breakdown reactor, a living proximal tubule cell bioreactor, and a biomimetic dermal patch into a continuous, wearable renal assist loop.
The system operates via two coupled fluidic loops:
 * Extracorporeal / Recirculating Dialysate Loop: Recirculates a sealed 1.5 L biocompatible fluid volume across the filtration membrane and catalytic recovery units at 30 to 60 mL/min.
 * Transdermal / Interstitial Sensing Loop: Extracts and monitors dermal interstitial fluid (ISF) at a passive rate of <50\ \mu\text{L/hr} for continuous biomarker tracking without inducing tissue compaction.
Fluid and Data Flow Mapping
 * Primary Fluid Input: Fluid enters the main manifold via native arterial pressure pulses (120/80\text{ mmHg}) and a transcutaneous magnetic impeller drive.
 * Synthetic Filtration Compartment: Raw fluid flows across a single-crystal Silicon Nanopore Membrane (SNM) coated with sub-5 nm zwitterionic poly(sulfobetaine methacrylate) (pSBMA) hydrogel.
 * Ultrafiltrate Stream: Protein-free ultrafiltrate (10\text{ to }30\text{ mL/hr}) is directed into the Proximal Tubule Bioreactor.
 * Bioreactor Reabsorption: Human RPTEC/TERT1 cells actively reabsorb essential ions (Na^+, K^+, HCO_3^-), glucose, and water back into the biological return line.
 * Spent Dialysate Stream: Concentrated uremic toxins flow into the PEC flow cell.
 * PEC Urea Breakdown & Gas Separation: Blue micro-LED irradiation (460\text{ nm}, 25\text{ mW/cm}^2) oxidizes urea on a nanostructured hematite/NiOOH photoanode into N_2 and CO_2 gases, which vent passively through a 0.2\ \mu\text{m} hydrophobic ePTFE membrane protected downstream by synthetic torus-margo check valves.
 * Regenerated Dialysate Return: Cleaned dialysate recirculates back to the SNM filtration manifold.
 * Sensor Data Pipeline: ISFET telemetry (K^+, pH, urea) and piezoresistive pressure transducers stream real-time metrics to a 32-bit RISC-V microcontroller running the ce_os deterministic Rust kernel.
 * Actuation Output: The controller drives piezo-acoustic surface acoustic wave (SAW) arrays (40\text{ kHz}) and actuates sub-microsecond electromagnetic safety line-block valves.
