3. Biological Subsystem
 * Cell Source & Characterization: Conditionally immortalized human proximal tubule epithelial cells (RPTEC/TERT1, ATCC CRL-4031). Cells maintain differentiated proximal tubule phenotypes, expressing Aquaporin-1 (AQP1), Na^+/K^+-ATPase, organic anion/cation transporters (OAT1/OCT2), and ZO-1 tight junctions.
 * ECM Substrate Coating: The interior quartz/PEEK bioreactor channels are sanitized and coated with a dual extracellular matrix layer consisting of Human Collagen Type IV (50\ \mu\text{g/mL}) and Fibronectin (10\ \mu\text{g/mL}) suspended in phosphate-buffered saline (PBS) at 37^\circ\text{C} for 2 hours.
 * Seeding Protocol: RPTEC/TERT1 cells are trypsinized (0.05\% Trypsin-EDTA), resuspended in DMEM/F-12 medium supplemented with 5\ \mu\text{g/mL} insulin, 5\ \mu\text{g/mL} transferrin, 5\text{ ng/mL} selenium, and 10\text{ ng/mL} human EGF, and seeded into the bioreactor at 1.5 \times 10^5\text{ cells/cm}^2. Static attachment is maintained for 48 hours at 37^\circ\text{C} in a 5\%\ CO_2 humidified incubator.
 * Fluid Shear Conditioning: Perfusion is initiated at 0.05\text{ dyne/cm}^2 and incrementally ramped over 12 hours until establishing continuous physiological fluid shear stress of 0.2\text{ to }0.5\text{ dyne/cm}^2. This shear rate induces 3D tubular lumen alignment, primary cilia expression, and tight junction maturation.
 * Viability & Integrity Maintenance: Monolayer tightness is monitored via inline Trans-Epithelial Electrical Resistance (TEER) sensor arrays. TEER values must remain \ge 150\ \Omega\cdot\text{cm}^2. If shear stress drops below 0.1\text{ dyne/cm}^2 or exceeds 0.8\text{ dyne/cm}^2, the ce_os controller auto-adjusts pump duty cycles to prevent cell delamination.
4. Synthetic Subsystem
 * Filtration Membrane Specs: MEMS single-crystal Silicon Nanopore Membrane (SNM) etched with uniform rectangular slit pores (5\text{ to }7\text{ nm} width, 45\text{ nm} length, porosity >10^9\text{ pores/cm}^2). Total active surface area is 180\text{ cm}^2, providing a hydraulic permeability of 120\text{ mL/hr/mmHg/m}^2 while retaining >99.5\% of serum albumin.
 * Zwitterionic Anti-Fouling Coating: Membrane surfaces undergo atom transfer radical polymerization (ATRP) to covalently graft a sub-5 nm poly(sulfobetaine methacrylate) (pSBMA) hydrogel monolayer. This layer forms an electrostatic hydration barrier that eliminates protein adsorption and platelet activation without systemic anticoagulants.
 * Biomimetic Architectural Upgrades:
   * Collembola Re-Entrant Structures: Mushroom-shaped overhanging nanostructures (200\text{ nm} height) are etched into channel entry zones to provide super-oleophobic non-wetting properties with breakout pressures >2.0\text{ bar}.
   * Ligia Exotica Open-Capillaries: Microchannels incorporate 50\ \mu\text{m} Hair-Like Protrusions (HLPs) and 100\ \mu\text{m} Paddle-Like Protrusions (PLPs) to drive passive capillary fluid distribution.
   * Torus-Margo Check Valves: Lithographically etched PDMS torus-margo valves (3.4\ \mu\text{m} torus diameter) provide passive elastohydrodynamic pressure limiting and instant gas-sealing upon detecting air bubbles.
 * Dialysate Regeneration Chemistry: Operates on a closed 1.5 L recirculating dialysate volume. Urea clearance is driven by a photoelectrocatalytic (PEC) reactor containing a nanostructured hematite (\alpha\text{-Fe}_2\text{O}_3) photoanode coated with a NiOOH catalyst. Under 460 nm blue micro-LED illumination (25\text{ mW/cm}^2), urea is oxidized into nitrogen and carbon dioxide gas:
Secondary sorbent layers containing 100\text{ g} zirconium phosphate and 50\text{ g} zirconium oxide scavenge trace free ammonium and phosphate ions.
 * Pumps & Flow Dynamics: Dual opposite-phase piezoceramic diaphragm pumps maintain dialysate recirculation at 30\text{ to }60\text{ mL/min}. Ultrafiltration/sensing extraction flow is maintained at 10\text{ to }30\text{ mL/hr}.
5. Fabrication & Assembly
 * Chassis CNC Machining: Machine the main housing from medical-grade PEEK stock. Integrate fractal ribbing geometry along interior walls to resist hydrostatic crushing forces.
 * Piezoelectric Transducer Bonding: Epoxy-bond thin-film AlN piezoceramic ring transducers to the outer titanium cassette housing using thermally conductive epoxy. Cure at 60^\circ\text{C} for 2 hours.
 * Membrane Sealing: Seat the pSBMA-coated SNM inside the titanium cassette using FKM fluoroelastomer compression gaskets. Torque titanium assembly screws to 0.8\text{ Nm} in a cross-star pattern.
 * PEC Cell Assembly: Mount the hematite/NiOOH photoanode inside the quartz flow cell. Position the 460 nm LED board 2.0\text{ mm} above the optical window and install the 0.2\ \mu\text{m} ePTFE degassing membrane over the exhaust manifold.
 * Plumbing Integration: Connect platinum-cured silicone tubing between components. Connect PVDF quick-disconnect couplings to external ports.
 * Cleanroom Sterilization: Assemble non-biological manifolds in an ISO Class 7 cleanroom. Sterilize PEEK housing and fluid lines via Ethylene Oxide (EtO); sterilize SNM cassettes via gamma irradiation (25\text{ kGy}).
 * Bioreactor Integration: Inoculate and mature the RPTEC/TERT1 cell cartridge under aseptic conditions in a laminar flow hood, then connect to the primary fluid circuit using PVDF aseptic couplings.
6. Control Electronics & Firmware
 * Sensors:
   * Piezoresistive Transmembrane Pressure (TMP) sensors (range 0\text{ to }300\text{ mmHg}, precision \pm 1\text{ mmHg}) placed pre- and post-filter.
   * Ion-Selective Field-Effect Transistors (ISFET) monitoring potassium (K^+, 3.0\text{ to }7.0\text{ mmol/L}), urea, and pH (6.8\text{ to }7.8).
   * Dual-wavelength optical leak detectors monitoring hemoglobin (415\text{ nm}) and micro-bubbles (650\text{ nm}, sensitivity >10\ \mu\text{m}).
 * Controller Architecture: 32-bit RISC-V dual-core microcontroller executing ce_os, a bare-metal, no_std Rust operating system kernel. All memory buffers are statically allocated at compile time to prevent heap fragmentation.
 * Control Loops: Executed on a hard real-time 10 ms control tick.
   * Defouling Loop: If TMP exceeds 18.0\text{ mmHg}, ce_os triggers the 40\text{ kHz} DF-IPSS piezo-acoustic SAW sweep protocol (15\text{ ms} active pulse / 85\text{ ms} rest duty cycle) capped strictly below 0.25\text{ W/cm}^2 to prevent erythrocyte hemolysis.
   * Urea Loop: Adjusts 460 nm LED intensity (5\text{ to }25\text{ mW/cm}^2) based on real-time ISFET urea conductivity readings.
 * Alarms & Fail-Safes:
   * Potassium Spike (K^+ > 6.2\text{ mmol/L}): Automatically throttles recirculation pumps and alerts user via BLE telemetry.
   * Air Embolism / Pressure Surge: The CE-OS Deterministic Safety Firewall actuates an electromagnetic bypass line-block within 9.15\text{ ns} using Rayleigh acoustic cavitation collapse logic.
